<!--
    GRTubeYou: the soft darkening behind the title and the metadata line.

    Two things were wrong with the text sitting directly on the video: a bright frame washed
    it out, and a busy one broke it up. This is the cheapest honest fix - a gradient that is
    strongest at the very top, where the title is, and gone before it reaches the picture's
    middle. No panel, no edge, no rectangle: the top of the frame is already a boundary, and a
    second one would read as a box.

    Alpha rather than a solid colour, so the video is never actually hidden - it only stops
    competing with the text. 0xB0 at the top edge falls to fully transparent at the bottom of
    this strip, which is a fifth of the screen: dark enough under the title, invisible by the
    time the picture proper begins.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient
        android:angle="270"
        android:startColor="#B0000000"
        android:centerColor="#66000000"
        android:endColor="#00000000"
        android:type="linear" />
</shape>